<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neuburg an der Donau</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Neuburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Neuburg an der Donau is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. From 1505 it was the capital of the principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palatinate-neuburg">Palatinate-Neuburg</a>, created for the grandsons of Duke George of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria-landshut">Bavaria-Landshut</a>. Otto Henry rebuilt its castle in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> style, and the town remained a Palatine residence until the line moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dusseldorf">Düsseldorf</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heidelberg">Heidelberg</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neuburg-an-der-donau.jpg" alt="Neuburg an der Donau" width="320" height="237" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Mendli at German Wikipedia. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schloss_Neuburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
